    {
      "format": "Monotype",
      "outdated": null,
      "overview": "",
      "comments": "<h3>Other Options</h3>\n<h4>Electric</h4>\n<p>Volt Switch can be used instead of Energy Ball to provide a pivoting move after setting up Sticky Web, but the loss of Energy Ball means that Galvantula can't hit Ground-types, especially <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/great-tusk/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Great Tusk</a>.</p>",
      "movesets": [
        {
          "name": "Entry Hazard Lead (Bug)",
          "pokemon": "Galvantula",
          "shiny": false,
          "gender": "DC",
          "levels": [],
          "description": "<p>Sticky Web Galvantula is a decent lead on Bug teams due to its ability to set Sticky Web up, allowing teammates such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/volcarona/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Volcarona</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/scizor/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Scizor</a> to sweep more easily. Thunder, combined with the accuracy boost from Compound Eyes, is Galvantula's strongest move, which hits Water-types such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/toxapex/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Toxapex</a> and deters Flying-type Defoggers such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/corviknight/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Corviknight</a>. Thunder Wave allows Galvantula to cripple faster threats such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/weavile/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Weavile</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/flutter-mane/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Flutter Mane</a>. Energy Ball gives Galvantula coverage against Ground-types such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/quagsire/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Quagsire</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/great-tusk/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Great Tusk</a>, Great Tusk in particular being another Pokemon that can remove Sticky Web. Volt Switch can be used instead of Energy Ball to provide a pivoting move after setting up Sticky Web, but the loss of Energy Ball means that Galvantula can't hit Ground-types, especially the aforementioned Great Tusk. Focus Sash gives Galvantula a guaranteed Sticky Web, attack, or chance to paralyze. The given EV spread with a Timid nature allows Galvantula to get up Sticky Web consistently while also maximizing its Special Attack in order to deal the most damage possible.</p>\n<p>Pokemon that benefit from Galvantula's Sticky Web are ideal partners for it. The aforementioned Volcarona and Scizor both appreciate their threats being slowed down so they can set up with Quiver Dance and Swords Dance, respectively. Scizor is able to take out <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/arcanine-hisui/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Hisuian Arcanine</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/glimmora/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Glimmora</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/weezing-galar/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Galarian Weezing</a>, while Volcarona outspeeds faster threats like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/greninja/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Greninja</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/iron-valiant/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Iron Valiant</a> under Sticky Web. <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/slither-wing/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Slither Wing</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/lokix/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Lokix</a> also appreciate Sticky Web, as it helps them wallbreak and revenge kill against normally faster threats, such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/ogerpon-hearthflame/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Ogerpon-H</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/gholdengo/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Gholdengo</a>, and Choice Specs <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/iron-moth/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Iron Moth</a>. Choice Scarf <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/kleavor/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Kleavor</a> is a great teammate for Galvantula because it can deal with Fire-types such as Ogerpon-H and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/moltres/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Moltres</a>. Kleavor's Stone Axe also pairs nicely with Galvantula's Sticky Web, as more entry hazards further help the sweepers and wallbreakers on the team, while also breaking <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/ceruledge/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Ceruledge</a>'s Focus Sash, which is a huge problem for Bug teams. <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/forretress/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Forretress</a> removes entry hazards with Rapid Spin, provides a strong physical wall on Bug teams, and is a slow pivot for Galvantula with Volt Switch to ensure its safe entry.</p>",
          "abilities": [
            "Compound Eyes"
          ],
          "items": [
            "Focus Sash"
