        {
          "name": "Sticky Web (Electric)",
          "pokemon": "Galvantula",
          "shiny": false,
          "gender": "DC",
          "levels": [],
          "description": "<p>With its high base Speed, Galvantula is an excellent lead due to it being the only consistent Sticky Web setter on Electric teams. Thunder, combined with the accuracy boost from Compound Eyes, is Galvantula's strongest move, which hits Water-types such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/toxapex/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Toxapex</a> and deters Flying-type Defoggers such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/corviknight/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Corviknight</a>. Bug Buzz is used to hit Pokemon that resist Thunder like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/hydreigon/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Hydreigon</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/latios/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Latios</a>, while Thunder Wave allows Galvantula to cripple faster threats such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/weavile/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Weavile</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/flutter-mane/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Flutter Mane</a>. Energy Ball gives Galvantula coverage against Ground-types such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/quagsire/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Quagsire</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/great-tusk/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Great Tusk</a>, which is valuable, as Great Tusk can remove Sticky Web. Focus Sash gives Galvantula a guaranteed chance to set Sticky Web, attack, or paralyze the opponent.</p>\n<p>Pokemon that can take advantage of Sticky Web are great teammates for Galvantula. <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/rotom-wash/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Rotom-W</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/zapdos/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Zapdos</a> both benefit from Sticky Web, as they can outspeed threats such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/iron-valiant/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Iron Valiant</a> and the <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/ogerpon/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Ogerpon</a> formes at -1 while also providing a Ground immunity. <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/raging-bolt/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Raging Bolt</a> especially benefits from Sticky Web, as its underwhelming Speed tier holds it back, and it appreciates the Speed drop from Sticky Web so it can set up and wallbreak more easily. <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/sandy-shocks/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Sandy Shocks</a> pairs well with Galvantula, forming an entry hazard-stacking core combining Sticky Web with its Stealth Rock and Spikes. <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/regieleki/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Regieleki</a> provides hazard removal for Electric teams with Rapid Spin and pivoting with Volt Switch so wallbreakers like the aforementioned Raging Bolt can come in repeatedly. Although <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/iron-hands/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Iron Hands</a> doesn't really benefit from Sticky Web, it is still a great teammate due to its high bulk and can take out threats that wall Galvantula, such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/tyranitar/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Tyranitar</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/goodra-hisui/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Hisuian Goodra</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/blissey/monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Blissey</a>. In return, Galvantula takes out Quagsire and Great Tusk for Iron Hands.</p>",
          "abilities": [
            "Compound Eyes"
          ],
