    {
      "format": "Ubers UU",
      "outdated": null,
      "overview": "",
      "comments": "",
      "movesets": [
        {
          "name": "Sticky Web",
          "pokemon": "Galvantula",
          "shiny": false,
          "gender": "DC",
          "levels": [],
          "description": "<p>Galvantula carves out a niche in Ubers UU thanks to it being the fastest available Sticky Web setter, having solid offenses, and having the ability to threaten out common forms of entry hazard control like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/great-tusk/ubers-uu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Great Tusk</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/mandibuzz/ubers-uu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mandibuzz</a>. Energy Ball gives Galvantula coverage against Ground-types like Great Tusk and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/landorus/ubers-uu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Landorus</a>, although Bug Buzz is an option to give it a secondary STAB option hit Pokemon like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/mewtwo/ubers-uu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mewtwo</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/arceus-dark/ubers-uu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Arceus-Dark</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/deoxys/ubers-uu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Deoxys</a>. Thunder Wave allows Galvantula to cripple Pokemon like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/zacian/ubers-uu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Zacian</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/kyurem-white/ubers-uu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Kyurem-W</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/arceus-poison/ubers-uu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Arceus-Poison</a> after setting up Sticky Web. Although Galvantula will not often Terastallize, Tera Ghost allows it to block Rapid Spin from Great Tusk and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/cyclizar/ubers-uu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Cyclizar</a>. Focus Sash guarantees Galvantula will set up Sticky Web and potentially fire off an attack or paralyze something afterwards. Galvantula should be exclusively used as a Sticky Web lead for hyper offense teams. The most obvious partners for Galvantula are Pokemon that appreciate having their faster offensive counters slowed down, as well as Pokemon commonly revenge killed by faster threats. As a result, Pokemon like Choice Specs Kyurem-W, Mewtwo, and Landorus all make solid teammates. Ghost-types like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/gholdengo/ubers-uu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Gholdengo</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/dragapult/ubers-uu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Dragapult</a> and Taunt users like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/arceus/ubers-uu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Arceus</a> formes can prevent Rapid Spin and Defog and keep Sticky Web up. Counter leads like Taunt Arceus-Dark, Deoxys, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/hatterene/ubers-uu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Hatterene</a> can prevent Sticky Web being set up and give Galvantula issues, so Pokemon like Hatterene and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/palafin/ubers-uu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Palafin</a> that can deal with these threats are good to have as partners.</p>",
